# Spin texture of an irradiated warped topological insulator surface

Debabrata Sinha

_The Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai 600 113, India_
_TIFR Centre for Interdisciplinary Sciences, Hyderabad 500075, India_

###### Abstract

A hexagonally warped topological-insulator surface state under off-resonant
circularly polarized light develops a novel spin texture that breaks the
conventional spin-momentum locking, dictated by the $C_{3v}$ symmetry group.

## 1 Model and Floquet Theory

\[H_{0}(\vec{k})=\hbar vk\left(k_{x}\sigma_{y}-k_{y}\sigma_{x}\right)+\frac{\lambda}{2}\left(k_{+}^{3}+k_{-}^{3}\right)\sigma_{z} \tag{1}\]

\[H(\vec{k},t)=H_{0}(\vec{k})+V(t) \tag{2}\]

\[V(t)=ev[A_{x}\sigma_{y}-A_{y}\sigma_{x}]+\frac{3e\lambda}{2\hbar}\left[k_{+}^{2}A_{+}+k_{-}^{2}A_{-}\right]\sigma_{z}+O(A^{2},A^{3})\]

\[H_{\mathrm{eff}}=H_{0}+\frac{[V_{-1},V_{+1}]}{\hbar\omega} \tag{3}\]

\[V_{-1}=i\alpha(i\sigma_{x}-\sigma_{y})+i\beta[2ik_{x}k_{y}-(k_{x}^{2}-k_{y}^{2})]\sigma_{z},\quad V_{+1}=V_{-1}^{\dagger}\]
\[\alpha=\frac{evA_{0}}{2},\qquad \beta=\frac{3e\lambda A_{0}}{2\hbar}\]

\[H_{\mathrm{eff}}=\hbar v[(k_{x}+K_{1})\sigma_{y}-(k_{y}+K_{2})\sigma_{x}]+\frac{\lambda}{2}(k_{+}^{3}+k_{-}^{3})\sigma_{z}+\Delta_{\omega}\sigma_{z} \tag{4}\]

\[K_{1}=-\frac{4\alpha\beta}{\hbar^{2}\omega v}(k_{x}^{2}-k_{y}^{2}),\quad K_{2}=\frac{8\alpha\beta}{\hbar^{2}\omega v}k_{x}k_{y},\quad \Delta_{\omega}=\frac{4\alpha^{2}}{\hbar\omega}\]

\[H_{\mathrm{eff}}=\begin{pmatrix}\Delta(k,\theta)&\hbar v(-ik_{-}+iak_{+}^{2})\\ \hbar v(ik_{+}-iak_{-}^{2})&-\Delta(k,\theta)\end{pmatrix} \tag{5}\]

\[\Delta(\vec{k},\theta)=\lambda k^{3}\cos(3\theta)+\Delta_{\omega}=\lambda(k_{x}^{3}-3k_{x}k_{y}^{2})+\Delta_{\omega},\qquad a=\frac{4\alpha\beta}{\hbar^{2}\omega v}\]

\[E(\vec{k})=s\sqrt{\left(\Delta(\vec{k},\theta)\right)^{2}+\hbar^{2}v^{2}\left(k^{2}+a^{2}k^{4}-2ak^{3}\cos(3\theta)\right)} \tag{6}\]

\[C_{s}^{2}=\left[1+\frac{\hbar^{2}v^{2}(k^{2}+a^{2}k^{4}-2ak^{3}\cos 3\theta)}{(E_{s}+\Delta(k,\theta))^{2}}\right]^{-1} \tag{8}\]

## 2 Spin Texture

\[S_{x}=\frac{\hbar}{2}C_{s}^{2}\frac{\hbar v[-4ak_{x}k_{y}-2k_{y}]}{E_{s}(k,\theta)+\Delta(k,\theta)} \tag{9}\]

\[S_{y}=\frac{\hbar}{2}C_{s}^{2}\frac{\hbar v[-2a(k_{x}^{2}-k_{y}^{2})+2k_{x}]}{E_{s}(k,\theta)+\Delta(k,\theta)} \tag{10}\]

\[S_{z}=\frac{\hbar}{2}C_{s}^{2}\left[1-\frac{\hbar^{2}v^{2}(k^{2}+a^{2}k^{4}-2ak^{3}\cos 3\theta)}{(E_{s}(k,\theta)+\Delta(k,\theta))^{2}}\right] \tag{11}\]

## 3 In-Plane Spin Density

\[S_{\mathrm{tot}}(k,\theta)=\frac{\hbar vk\sqrt{1+a^{2}k^{2}-2ak\cos(3\theta)}}{\sqrt{\hbar^{2}v^{2}k^{2}(1+a^{2}k^{2}-2ak\cos 3\theta)+\Delta^{2}(k,\theta)}}\,C_{s}^{2} \tag{12}\]

\[S_{\mathrm{tot}}(k,\theta)=\frac{\hbar vk}{\sqrt{\hbar^{2}v^{2}k^{2}+\lambda^{2}k^{6}\cos^{2}(3\theta)}}\qquad (a=0,\ \Delta_{\omega}=0) \tag{13}\]

## 4 Out-of-Plane Spin

\[S_{z}=\pm\frac{\hbar}{2}\frac{\lambda(k_{x}^{3}-3k_{x}k_{y}^{2})}{\sqrt{\hbar^{2}v^{2}k^{2}+\lambda^{2}(k_{x}^{3}-3k_{x}k_{y}^{2})^{2}}}\qquad (a=0,\ \Delta_{\omega}=0) \tag{14}\]

## 5 Angle of Deviation

\[\delta_{\omega}=\cos^{-1}\left[\frac{-ak\sin(3\theta)}{\sqrt{1+a^{2}k^{2}-2ak\cos(3\theta)}}\right]-\frac{\pi}{2} \tag{15}\]

\[H_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\Gamma-M}=\hbar v[ak_{y}^{2}\sigma_{y}-k_{y}\sigma_{x}]+\Delta_{\omega}\sigma_{z} \tag{16}\]

\[H_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\Gamma-K}=\hbar v(k_{x}-ak_{x}^{2})\sigma_{y}+(\lambda k_{x}^{3}+\Delta_{\omega})\sigma_{z} \tag{17}\]

\[H_{hw}=i\xi(k_{+}^{5}\sigma_{+}-k_{-}^{5}\sigma_{-})\quad\text{(higher-order warping perturbation)}\]
